# Task 2: NumPy Arrays and Numerical Computation

# 1. Objective
To use NumPy arrays to analyse 24 hourly temperature readings.

## 2. Inputs
The program uses 24 temperature readings measured in degrees Celsius.

## 3. Mathematical Operations
- Calculate the mean temperature using `np.mean()`.
- Calculate the minimum using `np.min()`.
- Calculate the maximum using `np.max()`.
- Convert Celsius to Fahrenheit using `F = 1.8C + 32`.

## 4. Original Output
Daily mean temperature: 23.12 C
Minimum temperature: 17.50 C
Maximum temperature: 29.40 C
First six Fahrenheit readings: [65.3  64.4  64.04 63.5  64.22 66.2 ]

## 5. Modified Input
I changed one temperature reading from 29.4°C to 35.0°C.

## 6. Observation
When I changed the temperature from 29.4°C to 35.0°C, the average temperature increased from 23.12°C to 23.35°C. The highest temperature increased from 29.4°C to 35.0°C. The lowest temperature stayed at 17.5°C. The first six Fahrenheit readings did not change.
## 7. Interpretation
The results show that changing one temperature can affect the average and highest temperatures. The lowest temperature stayed the same because I did not change it. NumPy helped me calculate the temperatures quickly and convert them to Fahrenheit.